{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:MassTheory.PlancherelTerm7Formulation","@type":"LeanModule","name":"MassTheory.PlancherelTerm7Formulation","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:Mathlib.Algebra.BigOperators.Group.Finset.Basic","lean:module:Mathlib.Analysis.SpecialFunctions.Log.Basic","lean:module:Mathlib.Data.Real.Basic"],"declarations":10,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.WedderburnMass.plancherel_term_7","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.WedderburnMass.plancherel_term_7","kind":"def","line":74,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/plancherel-term-7-formulation.lean#L74-L79","doc":"**Plancherel Term 7 functional.**  Sum of curvature-rank-k log\nfunctionals over k ≥ 4. ","formalizes":[{"@id":"block:prop:plancherel-term-7-formulation","label":"prop:plancherel-term-7-formulation","md":"quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/plancherel-term-7-formulation.md"}],"signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.WedderburnMass.log_unbounded","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.WedderburnMass.log_unbounded","kind":"theorem","line":63,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/plancherel-term-7-formulation.lean#L63-L72","doc":"**Logarithmic unbounding lemma.**  For any M ≥ 0 there exists a\ncharacter value c with |c| > 0 such that log|c| > M.\nThis is why the bounded weight sum can produce unbounded\nlog-functional values when binned by stratum. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.WedderburnMass.phi_k","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.WedderburnMass.phi_k","kind":"def","line":48,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/plancherel-term-7-formulation.lean#L48-L52","doc":"The curvature-rank-k log functional. ","signature